-- title:
--   Descended level field: jmatĥ transcendental and F₀ finite, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over the residue field of $A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with $\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the geometric $j$-generator in the supersingular $j$-set), assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ via `hle`, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of the base-changed full level-$M'$ field along $A$ to the residue-field function field, compatible via `hR₀` with coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series over $A$. Further data: an element $\pi\in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$; an index $\zeta$ of a primitive $q$-th root of unity; families $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$, subject to: the explicit description of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ as the ratios of Laurent series over $A$ with denominator of nonzero reduction, transitivity of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-action through $\mathrm{redQ}$ and $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$, permutation of the $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ by each $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; for $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$, that constants of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ are exactly $A$, a compatibility `hSS_over` relating $R_0$-integral functions whose $j$-nonnegative orders force nonnegative orders to membership in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ together with residues at $s$ computing residues in $A$, invariance of each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ under all these automorphisms, and existence in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ of an element $t$ with $t-a$ a unit for every $a\in A$. Finally, a subfield $K_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ algebraic over it and $\pi\in K_0$; a henselian discrete valuation domain $A_0$ with an injective local ring homomorphism $\iota:A_0\to A$ whose image is $A\cap K_0$ and which is surjective onto the residue field of $A$, with uniformiser $\varpi_0$ satisfying $\iota\varpi_0=\pi$; the subfield $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of those elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, containing the element $\hat\jmath$ obtained from the coefficient embedding of $\mathrm{jq}$; and an $A_0$-algebra structure on $F_0$ whose structure map is $\iota$ followed by the inclusion of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. The conclusion is twofold: every polynomial $p$ over $A_0$ with $p(\hat\jmath)=0$ in $F_0$ is the zero polynomial, and $F_0$ is finite-dimensional over the subfield of $F_0$ generated by the image of $A_0$ together with $\hat\jmath$.
--
--   This is the transcendence-and-finiteness input for the descended Igusa-level function field at the prime $q=2$: over the descent base $K_0$, $A_0$ the modular invariant $\hat\jmath$ generates a rational subfield over which the descended field $F_0$ is finite. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_valuationSubring_localization_chartAlg_of_not_mem_descent_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_valuationSubring_localization_chartAlg_of_not_mem_descent_of_eq_two) in the construction of semistable charts on the full-level modular curve, and rests on the existence of an admissible descent base together with the general linear-disjointness statement `transcendental_and_finiteDimensional_adjoin_levelField`.
